issue_context.body:
Context https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/100206#issuecomment-2016856746

## Repro

```csharp
using System.Runtime.InteropServices;
using System.Runtime.CompilerServices;

Console.WriteLine(Unsafe.SizeOf<MyStruct>());

[StructLayout(LayoutKind.Explicit, Size = 9)]
struct MyStruct
{
    [FieldOffset(0)]
    public byte[] a;
    [FieldOffset(8)]
    public byte b;
}
```

## Expected result (on x64)

16

## Actual result

9

review_comments:
The `classLayoutSize` is only respected for value types by the runtime type loader: https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/8c68710084b861c44b6868c0bd972ce24aed55dd/src/coreclr/vm/methodtablebuilder.cpp#L8832-L8835

We should update the logic above to match, something like:
```
if (type.IsValueType)
{
    if (classLayoutSize != 0)
    {
       instanceSize = LayoutInt.Max(instanceSize, new LayoutInt(classLayoutSize));
    }
    else
    {
        instanceSize = LayoutInt.AlignUp(instanceSize, alignment, target);
    }
}
```

Repro:

```
using System.Runtime.InteropServices;
using System.Runtime.CompilerServices;

for (;;)
{
    var start = GC.GetAllocatedBytesForCurrentThread();
    GC.KeepAlive(new MyClass());
    Console.WriteLine(GC.GetAllocatedBytesForCurrentThread() - start);
}

[StructLayout(LayoutKind.Explicit, Size = 1000)]
class MyClass
{
    [FieldOffset(0)]
    public byte[] a;
    [FieldOffset(8)]
    public byte b;
}
```

Prints 32 with regular CoreCLR and 1016 with native AOT.
